    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **262 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the household-uniqueness rule for creating owners. Creating an owner is now rejected with **409 Conflict** when another owner has the same last name and the same address (compared case-insensitively with collapsed whitespace), unless the request sets `sharesHousehold: true`.\n\nFollowing the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions (not Spring MVC):\n\n**New pipeline step**\n- `EnsureOwnerHouseholdUnique` \u2014 reads the validated `@Val OwnerFieldsDto`, returns early when `sharesHousehold` is true, otherwise scans existing owners and throws when a normalized last-name + address match is found. Normalization = trim, collapse internal whitespace to a single space, lower-case (`Locale.ROOT`).\n- Wired into `owners.POST.yml` between `ensureTelephoneUnique` and `build` (governed by the same transaction), so a clash is a 409 before any row is persisted.\n\n**New escalation (409 handler)**\n- `DuplicateHouseholdException` (checked) + `DuplicateHouseholdExceptionHandler` responding `409` with a `ProblemDetail`, plus its `officefloor/escalation/*.yml`, mirroring the existing `DuplicateTelephoneException` pattern.\n\n**Schema**\n- Added a write-only `sharesHousehold` boolean to the `OwnerFields` OpenAPI schema (generates the DTO getter; excluded from responses).\n\n**Tests** (`OwnerRestControllerV1Tests`)\n- Added `createOwnerRejectsDuplicateHousehold` (409 via case/whitespace variant of the seeded Franklin household) and `createOwnerAllowsSharedHouseholdWhenAcknowledged` (201 with `sharesHousehold:true`).\n- Two pre-existing success tests (`createOwnerSuccess`, `createOwnerNormalizesTelephoneToE164`) created a Franklin at *110 W. Liberty St.* \u2014 the exact seeded household \u2014 which now legitimately conflicts under the new rule. I gave them distinct addresses so they still exercise their original intent (successful create / telephone normalization) without a spurious collision. PUT/update tests were unaffected since the rule is create-only.\n\nOne design note: the check uses `ownerRepository.findAll()` and compares in Java, because collapsing whitespace can't be expressed portably in the repository query layer, and it keeps the rule consistent across the JPA/JDBC/Spring-Data implementations.",
